content.text:
You must return exactly this format:

Saw you've been [Job Title] at [Company Name] since [Start Year] - kudos for leading [responsibility] at a [Company Age]-year-old company with [Company Size] employees.

Quick question - with [Company Name] covering [Service Lines], are your workers' comp and benefits costs where you want them, or is there room to put more money back in your pocket?
Rules:

[Job Title] = use 
{{2.data.data[].job_title}}
but trim to 3 words max
[Company Name] = 
{{2.data.data[].job_company_name}}
[Start Year] = extract year from 
{{2.data.data[].job_start_date}}
[responsibility] = if title has "vision/strategy" = "strategy", if "operations" = "operations", else = "growth"
[Company Age] = 2025 minus 
{{2.data.data[].job_company_founded}}
[Company Size] = 

convert size (1001-5000 = "1,000+", 51-200 = "200+")
[Service Lines] = 
{{2.data.data[].experience[].company.size}}
Use shortened like (IT, etc)
{{1.`13`}}
{{1.`12`}}
{{1.`11`}}

Perfect example:
Saw you've been CVO at Equiliem since 2022 - kudos for leading strategy at a 52-year-old company with 1,000+ employees.

Quick question - with Equiliem covering Industrial, IT, Health Care & Engineering placements, are your workers' comp and benefits costs where you want them, or is there room to put more money back in your pocket?"
